      "writtenOn": "2025-05-15T17:59:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Every FF-A version since 1.0 requires SMCCC 1.2. However before FF-A 1.2 only x0-x7 were used, and x8+ must be preserved. FF-A 1.2 and up uses x0-x17 so the registers that needs to be preserved depend on the FF-A version, not the SMCCC version.",
      "revId": "351d8f4ba812ec19a57bf26b1f0c844fd4847337",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9ef16579_c226b800",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1146,
      "author": {
        "id": 1807569
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-16T01:46:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e FF-A 1.2 and up uses x0-x17 so the registers that needs to be preserved depend on the FF-A version\n\nOn FF-A 1.2, it also depends on whether `FFA_MSG_SEND_DIRECT_REQ` or `FFA_FN64_MSG_SEND_DIRECT_REQ` was called.\n\nIn the former (SMC32/HVC32 on Aarch64) case, x8-x17 must indeed be preserved.\n\nIn the latter (SMC64/HVC64) case: \n- x8-x17 SBZ if the function completed with `FFA_FN64_MSG_SEND_DIRECT_RESP`, and \n- x2-x17 MBZ if it completed with `FFA_SUCCESS`.",
      "parentUuid": "f8bd7be0_788d1548",
      "revId": "351d8f4ba812ec19a57bf26b1f0c844fd4847337",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
